From: François Guerraz <kubrick@fgv6.net>
Subject: [PATCH] net: ethernet: qualcomm: ppe: let flows into the switch 
 leave with their bridge's MAC

A flow into the switch leaves with the bridge's MAC as its source (the
flowtable's Ethernet mangle), and the bridge's MAC need not be the
conduit's: on the GL-BE9300 it is not, and every such flow was declined.
The source MAC comes from the egress L3 interface, so give each such MAC
(up to four) an L3 interface of its own, past the PPPoE ones: the egress
entry carries the MAC, the ingress entry the port's MTU and no routing.
Accept it only for a DSA egress whose bridge has that MAC. Both are
written empty and read back when the last flow using them goes, or when
setting them up fails; a slot whose set-up or clearing does not read
back is not used again until offload is enabled again. That such an
interface, bound to no port and not routing, gives a nexthop its source
MAC is a bench hypothesis (HB). Saved and restored with the rest.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
